for anyone stumbling across this:
quick hacky workaround via scripting

Set the Max Log Files value in Project Settings to something higher than what you actually want, like 128.

Then call this function on game startup to keep 32 log versions:
```GDScript
# HACK: circumvents bug in log file rotation, check if this is fixed in Godot 4.4
func cleanup_logs():
	var keep_logs = 32
	var dir = DirAccess.open("user://logs/")
	if not dir:
		return
		
	var files = []
	dir.list_dir_begin()
	var file = dir.get_next()
	
	while file != "":
		if file.ends_with(".log") and file != "godot.log":
			files.append(file)
		file = dir.get_next()
	
	if files.size() <= keep_logs:
		return
		
	# Sort by timestamp in filename
	files.sort()
	
	# Delete oldest files until keep_logs remain
	for i in range(files.size() - keep_logs):
		dir.remove("user://logs/" + files[i])
```
